        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: stateful notes widget — the first consumer of widget write-back",
        "body": "> A notes pad on your dashboard that actually saves — and the pattern every stateful builtin after it will follow.\n\nCloses #101146. **Stacked on #101329 (widget write-back)**, which is itself stacked on #101098 — targets `main` with a cumulative diff; review `notes.ts` + the `buildBuiltinContext` host change as the delta beyond #101329.\n\n## What's in this PR\n\n- **`builtin:notes`** — an editable notes/todo pad. Content hydrates from persisted state on mount and saves on debounced input (~500 ms), so it survives reloads and stays consistent across two open browsers (the write-back broadcast triggers refetch).\n- **A host-bound state accessor for builtins** — the piece that makes this safe and reusable. `BuiltinWidgetContext` gains an optional `state` accessor (`get`/`set`), and the dashboard view now builds the context **per widget** (`buildBuiltinContext`), closing over the host's own `widget.id` when it calls `dashboard.widget.state.get`/`.set`. A widget renderer never names a widget id — it can only ever touch its own state. This mirrors the trust model of the sandboxed path in #101329 (parent binds the id), applied to trusted builtins.\n- **Graceful degradation** — with no connected client there's no `state` accessor, and the pad renders read-only with a hint instead of silently dropping writes.\n\n## How it works\nBuiltins render in the trusted Control UI, so they use the write-back gateway RPCs directly rather than the sandbox's postMessage bridge — but the id-binding discipline is identical: the host supplies `widget.id`, never the renderer. The persist test drives the real `buildBuiltinContext` (not a hand-rolled mock) and asserts the RPC receives `{ widgetId: \"notes-42\", state: … }` — the id-binding itself is under test. State lives in the per-widget jailed store from #101329 (64 KB cap, atomic writes, separate from `workspace.json`).\n\nNo new dependency — `pnpm-lock.yaml` unchanged.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** Operators want a scratchpad/todo on their dashboard, but before write-back (#101137/#101329) any editable widget reset on reload — and there was no pattern for a *builtin* to persist state safely. This adds a stateful notes builtin plus the host-bound per-widget state accessor that makes it (and future stateful builtins) possible.\n**Evidence:** `pnpm vitest run src/lib/dashboard` → 98 passed, including the four new notes cases (editable render, hydrate from mocked `state.get`, debounced persist through the real host-built context asserting the host-bound `widget.id`, and the read-only no-client fallback); `pnpm ui:i18n:check` clean; `pnpm ui:build` and full type-aware oxlint clean.\n",
